  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "f1",
      "text": "Many clouds contain supercooled water droplets that stay liquid below freezing but are too small to fall.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s2",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "definition"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2",
      "text": "Seeding releases particles such as silver iodide or dry ice into clouds from aircraft or ground generators, helping ice crystals form.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s1",
        "s2",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "cause_effect"
    },
    {
      "id": "f3",
      "text": "Ice crystals grow as water freezes onto them and fall as snow or rain once heavy enough.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s2",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "cause_effect"
    },
    {
      "id": "f4",
      "text": "In 1946 General Electric scientist Vincent Schaefer dropped dry ice from a plane into a cloud and snow fell from it.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s3",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "event"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5",
      "text": "Cloud seeding cannot create clouds; it only works when suitable clouds are already present.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s1",
        "s2"
      ],
      "kind": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": "f6",
      "text": "Measuring the effect of seeding is hard because no one knows how much rain would have fallen without it.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s2",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": "f7",
      "text": "Under the right conditions, seeding may increase precipitation modestly (roughly 5 to 15 percent, if it works).",
      "source_ids": [
        "s1",
        "s4"
      ],
      "kind": "number"
    },
    {
      "id": "f8",
      "text": "Cloud seeding cannot end a drought on its own.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s1"
      ],
      "kind": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": "f9",
      "text": "Taiwan suffered its worst drought in decades in 2021, and reservoir levels fell very low.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s8"
      ],
      "kind": "event"
    },
    {
      "id": "f10",
      "text": "Irrigation water to rice fields in Hsinchu, Miaoli and Taichung was stopped for the 2021 spring crop to save water for homes and industry.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s6"
      ],
      "kind": "event"
    },
    {
      "id": "f11",
      "text": "Officials said farmers whose crops were affected by cuts in irrigation would be compensated.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s7"
      ],
      "kind": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": "f12",
      "text": "In April 2021, Taiwan's air force used a C-130 transport plane to seed clouds above Miaoli County and Taichung during the drought.",
      "source_ids": [
        "s5"
      ],
      "kind": "event"
    }
  ],
  "datasets": [],
